<title>TURKEY: Turk Akbank Q1 net up at 18.4 trln lira.</title>
<headline>Turk Akbank Q1 net up at 18.4 trln lira.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jan-March 1997 provisional</p>
<p>(billion lira unless stated)</p>
<p>    Per share profit (lira)  1,022.57 vs     955.57</p>
<p>    Net profit		  18,406.20 vs   5,733.44</p>
<p>    Net interest income     35,076.75 vs  11,310.72</p>
<p>    Net non-interest expense 8,944.15 vs   3,227.80</p>
<p>    Provisions for bad loans   148.53 vs	51.64</p>
<p>    Loans			183,985.52 vs  66,983.60</p>
<p>    Deposits		   389,379.72 vs 167,112.23</p>
<p>    Loans borrowed	     3,432.13 vs   1,696.81</p>
<p>    Equity			51,591.97 vs  23,964.90</p>
<p>    Capital		     18,000.00 vs   6,000.00</p>
<p>NOTE - Akbank T.A.S. is one of Turkey's leading commercial banks, owned largely by industrial Sabanci conglomerate.</p>
<p>It distributed a 21.6 trillion lira cash dividend -- 1,200 lira per 1,000 lira nominal-valued share -- from 1996 profits in April.</p>
<p>The bank also raised its capital to 50 trillion lira by issuing 0.7777 bonus and one right for one existing share in April.</p>
<p>The figures above do not take into account Turkey's 77 percent annual inflation in March.</p>
<p>-- Istanbul newsroom +90-212-2750875.</p>
</text>
